    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:714f66f1-240b-4273-a9c7-23497efd0182",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:714f66f1-240b-4273-a9c7-23497efd0182/9847d8d1-ef20-4ccc-b9c7-de36e879b974/16",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:714f66f1-240b-4273-a9c7-23497efd0182/9847d8d1-ef20-4ccc-b9c7-de36e879b974/24",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:714f66f1-240b-4273-a9c7-23497efd0182/9847d8d1-ef20-4ccc-b9c7-de36e879b974/32",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:714f66f1-240b-4273-a9c7-23497efd0182/9847d8d1-ef20-4ccc-b9c7-de36e879b974/48"
      },
      "displayName": "Justin Simpson",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A714f66f1-240b-4273-a9c7-23497efd0182",
      "timeZone": "America/Vancouver"
     },
     "body": "<p>I have updated the wiki page at <a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FF/Export+Format\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FF/Export+Format</a> with some more information about how to perform a basic test with the Camel Serializer.  </p>\n\n<p>I can add more detailed installation instructions, for situations when the user is not using the vagrant box.  But I think those instructions should be added to <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4-exts/fcrepo-camel-toolbox\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4-exts/fcrepo-camel-toolbox</a> perhaps, rather than to this wiki page.  And I am not sure extra install instructions are required.  </p>\n\n<p>I assume the point of this ticket is to document a reproducible test case, and the output of the Serializer.  That might mean that this ticket can be closed now?  Happy to add more info if anything else would be useful.</p>",
